{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg --files src/cljc/yin/repl | rg -v '/(main|dht|query|store|state|index)\\\\.cljc\"'$'\"' | xargs rg -n 'dao\\\\.jing\\\\.dht|dao\\\\.space\\\\.dht|yin\\\\.repl\\\\.dht|:dht\\\\b|dht/'; sed -n '23,54p' src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/interpreter.cljc; rg -n 'link/|config/|:head-fn|:publish-opts|store/durable' src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc; rg -n 'jing/' src/cljc/yin/repl/query.cljc; rg -n 'deftest.*|ticker|twenty|400|eight|acknowledg' test/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc | tail -65; rg -n 'deftest' test/yin/repl/dht_head_test.cljc | tail -25\"","aggregated_output":"   re-read and re-attempted on a later round, and `abandon` is the\n   shell's.  No clock, no atom, no global: every input is an argument or\n   a composition value, and every outcome is plain data.\n\n   A DHT link source (docs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.md 4.1) holds no\n   handle: each serve round receives the shell's `dao.space.dht` node\n   and answers the node after it.  A resolved name whose closure is not\n   loaded starts its load (`yin.vm.linker.dht/load-module`) and reports\n   the link `:pending`, naming the manifest it waits on; the node's own\n   step fetches.  A failed load is refused in its section 9 shape and\n   forgotten; a loaded one has its dependency bindings checked, then\n   links over a local runtime on the node's store, asking no peer.\"\n  (:require [clojure.string :as str]\n            [dao.jing.content :as content]\n            [dao.space.dht :as dht]\n            [dao.stream :as stream]\n            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ring]\n            [yin.vm.linker :as linker]\n            [yin.vm.linker.admission :as admission]\n            [yin.vm.linker.dht :as linker.dht]\n            [yin.vm.linker.sign :as sign]))\n\n\n(def pair-capacity\n  \"Declared capacity of each link-pair medium, in elements.  The shell\n   appends one request per require, and a response medium a receiver\n   never drains answers `gap` (an evicted request is never re-read), so\n   the bound is generous and the eviction it guards against is a host\n   assembly defect, not an operating condition.\"\n  1024)\n\n\n255:       \"  (require (quote yin.link)), then (yin.link/publish (quote m)\"\n257:       \" indexed code under the --dht-key principal, and (yin.link/names)\"\n772:   (`:head-fn`, yin.repl.store): every session the store outlives\n775:  (let [linker (link/make source)\n792:                                   :publish-opts (:publish-opts index-store)\n793:                                   :after-publish (:head-fn index-store)})\n888:   `(yin.link/publish ...)` is refused and the node still reads, resolves,\n943:         link-source (link/composition\n1288:   indexer a `yin.link/publish` committed its name envelopes through.\"\n1303:  {:authority (link/authority (:link-source state))\n1357:                       (link/round (assoc (:linker state)\n1410:                                    \" (link \" (pr-str (:yin.link/id p))\n1471:           retired (link/retire (:linker state')\n1472:                                (link/run-descriptor (:base parked) vm))]\n1507:                                              :link-id (:yin.link/id p)})\n1846:           (store/durable? (:index-store state))\n1860:  (let [linker (link/reconfigure (:linker state) admission)]\n1872:      (let [p (config/parse-trust p)\n1904:                   (if (store/durable? (:index-store state))\n2069:  (let [served (link/round (assoc (:linker state)\n2205:                         :link-id (:yin.link/id p)\n701:          (not (jing/segment-address? manifest))\n493:  a-refused-manifest-is-reported-unacknowledged-and-cancel-ends-it\n523:        (is (str/includes? first-line \"NOT acknowledged\") first-line)\n535:(deftest a-publication-with-publishing-off-is-reported-and-sends-nothing\n542:            [shells _ lines] (run-until [shell] peers 0 400\n543:                                        #(line-with % \"acknowledged\"))]\n544:        (is (line-with lines \"NOT acknowledged\"))\n554:(deftest a-publication-short-of-peers-is-reported-with-why-at-the-deadline\n562:                                            #(line-with % \"acknowledged\"))]\n563:        (is (line-with lines \"NOT acknowledged\"))\n586:(deftest a-reader-given-a-manifest-hydrates-then-queries-the-remote-index\n631:(deftest hydration-is-a-directory-s-first-head-write-at-its-own-sequence\n703:(deftest a-manifest-no-peer-holds-refuses-the-reader\n725:(deftest the-step-owner-admits-no-line-while-hydrating\n776:(deftest a-socket-that-cannot-bind-refuses-and-stops-the-shell\n805:(deftest the-repl-queries-a-remote-index-through-the-same-plain-path\n874:(deftest a-plain-join-and-the-repl-store-exclude-each-other\n1021:(deftest\n1070:(deftest an-unrelated-node-event-causes-no-re-check\n1104:(deftest a-function-policy-counts-only-re-checks-of-this-run\n1138:(deftest a-keep-policy-never-ends-a-dht-run\n1161:(deftest\n1233:(deftest\n1258:(deftest a-defective-closure-raises-descriptor-defect-with-its-code\n1290:(deftest a-load-that-cannot-ask-raises-unaskable-with-the-outcome\n1326:(deftest a-dependency-binding-that-is-not-ok-raises-before-any-install\n1402:(deftest a-require-of-a-failed-candidate-s-address-leaves-it-to-the-follower\n1412:                                          :repair-max-ticks 400})\n1447:(deftest a-require-of-a-failed-index-load-made-by-hand-leaves-it-in-place\n1467:(deftest a-require-of-a-loading-or-loaded-record-of-another-kind-is-refused\n1518:(deftest all-four-vms-link-the-closed-corpus-over-the-dht\n1573:(deftest load-module-and-module-status-answer-through-the-plain-functions\n1594:(deftest both-load-operations-answer-a-refusal-as-data\n1635:(deftest a-dht-store-refuses-a-second-content-source\n1647:(deftest the-banner-and-help-say-a-require-may-fetch-from-peers\n1718:(deftest\n1796:(deftest\n1835:(deftest\n1923:   the re-check its load events call for, as the host ticker does), every\n2035:(deftest\n2049:        (is (= :acknowledged (:result report)) (pr-str (dissoc report :failed)))\n2088:(deftest\n2089:  ^:slow rounds-larger-than-the-pending-write-bound-are-acknowledged-never-busy\n2090:  (slow/guard \"rounds-larger-than-the-pending-write-bound-are-acknowledged-never-busy\"\n2115:                      (is (= (repeat 8 :acknowledged) (mapv :result reports)))\n2143:(deftest\n2230:              (is (= :acknowledged (:result again)) (pr-str again))\n2234:                                 \"acknowledged: sent to 2 peers\")))\n2253:(deftest retry-at-the-prompt-brings-the-same-repair-forward\n2267:        (is (= :acknowledged (:result again)) (pr-str again))\n2274:(deftest\n2275:  a-refused-manifest-is-unacknowledged-and-repaired-the-same-way\n2296:        (is (= :unacknowledged (:result report)))\n2299:        (is (= :acknowledged (:result again)) (pr-str again))\n2307:;; Peers that never accept: twenty rounds, the prompt and the ticker\n2310:(deftest\n2311:  ^:slow with-peers-that-never-accept-twenty-rounds-report-and-the-ticker-idles\n2313:    \"with-peers-that-never-accept-twenty-rounds-report-and-the-ticker-idles\"\n2347:             idle (reduce (fn [w _] (step w)) (assoc w :moved []) (range 400))]\n2349:            (is (every? #(str/includes? % \"NOT acknowledged\") firsts))\n2350:            (is (not-any? #(str/includes? % \"acknowledged: sent\") (:lines idle))\n2351:                \"no event ever reports acknowledged\")\n2352:            (testing \"between repair cycles the ticker returns to its idle cadence\"\n2365:(deftest\n2421:             _ (is (= :acknowledged (:result (event-of w :p :republished\n2469:(deftest\n16:            [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n204:(deftest the-token-prints-once-when-the-board-is-bound\n229:(deftest no-board-means-no-token\n269:(deftest ^:slow a-reader-follows-requires-moves-and-restarts-from-heads-edn\n354:(deftest abandon-ends-a-first-contact-require\n384:(deftest the-write-precedes-the-install\n429:(deftes